<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 0.7 pct in Aug 1-20 - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 0.7 pct in Aug 1-20 - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 813 million zlotys, or 0.7 percent, in the August 1-20 period to 120.41 billion after a 2.3-percent rise in July, preliminary central bank figures showed.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		  AUG 1-20  JULY	     AUG 95</p>
<p> change (pct)			     0.7	2.3		3.3</p>
<p> Money in bln zlotys		  120.41   119.60(119.61)  93.47</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in PLN bln)    22.09    21.97	    21.03</p>
<p>  National currency		    98.32    97.63 (97.64)  72.44</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		  22.59    22.49	    17.54</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector  66.85    65.16 (65.18)  54.90</p>
<p>NOTE: Revised figures in brackets. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
